<%# The embed, from TradingView's own generator. The copyright div and the 32px
    the container reserves for it are theirs, not decoration: the terms require
    the attribution to remain as it was designed (D66).

    The loader's <script> is built by tradingview_embed_controller rather than
    printed here, so the config travels as an attribute ERB escapes and no
    database value is ever marked html_safe.

    Only MACD is preset. `studies` takes ids without inputs, so a moving average
    would arrive at its default period — an MA200 cannot be asked for here, and
    shipping a default-period MA labelled as the long one would be a lie. The
    reader adds it from the widget's own Indicadores menu. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "asset_tradingview" do %>
  <div class="tradingview-widget-container mt-4" style="height: 420px"
       data-controller="tradingview-embed"
       data-tradingview-embed-config-value="<%= tradingview_config(@asset) %>">
    <div class="tradingview-widget-container__widget" style="height: calc(100% - 32px)"></div>
    <div class="tradingview-widget-copyright text-xs text-fg-subtle">
      <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/<%= @asset.symbol %>/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">
        <span class="text-primary"><%= @asset.symbol %></span>
      </a><span> by TradingView</span>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
